The attached image presents flow cytometry histograms demonstrating the effect of Nano-11 on the expression of costimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on dendritic cells (DCs). As explained in Figure 6 of the provided PDF, bone marrow-derived DCs incubated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) for two days show increased expression of CD80 and CD86 compared to medium control (gray line), evidenced by the rightward shift in the black peaks. A subtle increase in CD40 expression is also visible. This indicates that Nano-11 effectively activates DCs, a crucial process for promoting an adaptive immune response.